  "config_source_text": "# Self-report sweep, pinned 2026-09-20.\n#\n# The grid is instrument-agnostic \u2014 only `instrument:` names what gets asked, so a\n# second experiment is a second file in this directory.\n#\n# Cells: 1 baseline + 4 personas x 3 system-prompt variants = 13.\n# Prompts: 45 targets x 3 forms x 3 paraphrases = 405 per cell.\n# Calls: 13 x 405 x n_samples.\n\nrun: self_report_v2\ninstrument: self_report\n\ninstrument_args:\n  # One wording per item this run. All three stay in forms.json; using one\n  # means paraphrase_agreement is not measurable, and the summary says so\n  # rather than reporting a spread of zero.\n  n_paraphrases: 1\n\nmodels:\n  # The OpenRouter slug, not the bare `gpt-4.1` registry key: that one routes\n  # to OpenAI directly and needs OPENAI_API_KEY. Same model, different path.\n  - openai/gpt-4.1\n\nroutes:\n  - system\n  # - system_facts_k4    # the ICL cell's facts in the system slot, unnamed;\n  # - system_facts_k32   # expands over facts_variants, not variants\n  # - icl_k4      # corpora are present for all four personas\n  # - icl_k32\n  # - sft         # needs configs/checkpoints.yaml entries; vader/curie pending\n\n# vader held back for now.\npersonas: [voldemort, stalin, curie]\n\n# Variants apply to the system route only; ICL and SFT have no prompt to vary.\n# default only for this run; minimal/roleplay deferred.\nvariants: [default]\n\n# Frames for the system_facts routes: default keeps the voice and persistence\n# clauses, minimal drops them. Both by default.\nfacts_variants: [default, minimal]\n\n# Not optional in practice: a persona's number only means something as a\n# difference from the same model with nothing induced.\nbaseline: true\n\nsampling:\n  n_samples: 5\n  temperature: 1.0\n  seed: 42\n  # Generation cap. A persona that preambles before the number gets truncated\n  # and scores unparsed, so this drives the unparsed rate directly.\n  max_tokens: 64\n\nconcurrency:\n  # Prompts within a cell run concurrently; cells run one at a time. The 429\n  # backoff in llm/provider.py is per-call and blind to siblings, so widening\n  # both axes buys rate-limit failures rather than speed. workers: 1 restores\n  # the repo's otherwise-sequential behaviour.\n  workers: 4\n",
